60,3,1,talk,May,,"Now that we've seen the options, I'm leaning towards the Open Kitchen. It solves the desk mess and the lunch commute, and it could be the social spark we need.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"I'm voting for the Quiet Room. Given how thin the walls are and the noise levels, we need a space that guarantees peace and doesn't add to the chaos.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,I believe the Meeting Space is the most prudent choice. It eliminates the unnecessary expense of outside rentals and provides the professional privacy we currently lack.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"I'm going with the Open Kitchen! It's way more fun, it saves us from those long lunch walks, and it's cheaper to fit out than a meeting room!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm voting for the Meeting Space. We really need a place for those difficult conversations, and it's the only option that actually fixes the privacy problem.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, a Quiet Room sounds a bit lonely, doesn't it? We need something that brings us together, not something that keeps us apart in silence.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,It's not about being lonely; it's about the fact that we are already too exposed. A space where we can actually focus without hearing everything through the walls is a necessity.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"While peace is a virtue, the data suggests our primary deficiency is a lack of a structured environment for collaboration and private discourse.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Sakura,,But a meeting room is just for work! We already work all day! Let's make it a place where we can actually relax and eat together!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, relaxing is important, but we can't relax if we're stressed because we have nowhere to talk privately. A Meeting Space gives us that essential boundary.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,"I still think the kitchen is the best bet for morale. If we have a place to gather, the ""difficult conversations"" might just happen more naturally and less awkwardly.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,Natural gatherings don't solve the problem of thin walls; they just make the noise constant. I can't support a kitchen when I'm the one hearing every single conversation.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is clear that we are divided between the desire for social warmth and the need for professional boundaries. However, the financial waste of outside hire is a fact we cannot ignore.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Sakura,,But we can use the money we save from outside hire to make the kitchen even better! Let's just go for the Open Kitchen!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I can't agree with that. We need a solution for the privacy issues and the awkwardness, and a kitchen just adds more noise to a room that already leaks sound.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,May,,I'll stick with my vote for the Open Kitchen. It's the only option that addresses the daily mess and the lunch struggle while giving us a heart for the office.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"My vote remains the Quiet Room. We need a sanctuary from the noise and the lack of privacy, not more reasons for the office to be loud.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Servas,,"I shall maintain my vote for the Meeting Space, as it is the most balanced solution for our professional needs and our budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm sticking with the Open Kitchen! It's the most exciting choice and it'll make everyone way happier during the day!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm staying with the Meeting Space. We need a place to actually connect and handle things privately, and that's the only way to fix our office culture.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
